        "question": "A data engineering team has a Lakeflow Job with the following task dependencies:\ningest_customers \u2500\u2500\u2192 build_silver_customers \u2500\u2500\u2510\n\u2193\nbuild_gold_sales\n\u2191\ningest_orders \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2192 build_silver_orders \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518\nDuring one execution:\nbuild_silver_customers completed successfully\nbuild_silver_orders failed after exhausting all configured retries\nLater, the engineering team notices that build_gold_sales still executed successfully but produced only partial downstream data.\nWhich Run if conditions on the dependencies to build_gold_sales could have caused this behavior?\nSelect TWO answers.",
        "Correct answer": "optionA, optionB",
        "explanation": "Lakeflow Jobs supports configurable Run if conditions on task dependencies. These conditions determine when downstream tasks execute based on the outcome of upstream tasks.\nCommon Run if conditions include:\nAll succeeded: All upstream dependencies must complete successfully. This is the default behavior.\nAt least one succeeded: The downstream task executes if at least one upstream dependency succeeds.\nNone failed: No upstream dependencies failed, and at least one dependency executed successfully.\nAll done: The downstream task executes after all upstream tasks finish, regardless of success or failure outcomes.\nAt least one failed: The downstream task executes if at least one upstream dependency fails.\nAll failed: The downstream task executes only if all upstream dependencies fail.\nIn this scenario:\nbuild_silver_customers succeeded\nbuild_silver_orders failed\nbuild_gold_sales still executed\nThis behavior could occur with:\nAt least one succeeded\nAll done\nBoth configurations can allow downstream tasks to execute even when upstream failures occur, potentially resulting in partial downstream data.\nResources",
